lines=['# Original-requirement traceability matrix','',f'Reviewed commit: `90724fea4152861499063b4f163d84c28348b0d3`. Original source: `../REQUIREMENTS.md`, SHA-256 `5242b663b3160ceb5c751363eecf9c607b59046dee3b4955118fd6b765733c1d`.','', 'Short-path convention: `issue-triage.md`/`issue-triage.lock.yml` are in `.github/workflows/`; `workflow.md` means `.github/workflows/issue-triage.md`; `SKILL.md`, `check_labels.py`, `render_comment.py` are under `.claude/skills/issue-triage/` (scripts under its `scripts/`); `post_triage_comment.py`/`prepare_agent_context.py` are in `scripts/`; `fetch_issues.py` is in `evals/tools/`; bare `cases/`, `results/`, `actual/` and `control-forced/` references are under the explicitly named `evals/golden/` case/results context. The case/run names identify exact saved records.', '', 'Every normative requirement and compound subrequirement is mapped below. Example workflows are alternatives. Repeated deliverable wording is retained so nothing disappears between the task and submission sections. References are repository-relative paths with physical lines, or exact saved case/run paths. `direct-checks.json`, `unit-tests.txt` and `reproduction-results.json` are new evidence in this review folder.', '', '**Status:** met = sufficient artifact/evidence for the assignment requirement; partial = unresolved substantive scope or human/external verification; missing = no required artifact/evidence found; not-applicable = explicit exemption. A met status is not a claim that every decision was correct or every control was stress-tested. No numeric grading rubric is inferred.','', '**Separate standards:** the assignment requires at least 10 historical inputs and one attack, including no-action cases and honest comparisons. The repository’s 90-run/k=3 shadow-deployment gates and later strict experiment gates are self-imposed acceptance standards, not new assignment minimums. Student explanation, commit selection, eLearn submission and access remain human responsibilities.','']
